<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The desktop shell (gajae-app-desktop) is a Rust binary hosting WKWebView.
    It runs no JIT of its own - WebKit's content and GPU processes are separate,
    Apple-signed XPC services - loads only system frameworks and its own
    statically linked code, and takes nothing from DYLD_* variables. So it
    carries none of the hardened-runtime exceptions the sidecar needs
    (entitlements.plist): allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory,
    allow-dyld-environment-variables, disable-library-validation. Granting
    those to the shell would only widen what a compromised shell could load.

    scripts/release/finalize-macos-app.mjs signs the outer app with this file
    and refuses a bundle whose shell still carries a sidecar exception
    (owner decision 2026-09-18, #129).
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
